// An abandoned mine's two levels, through its shaft: from the lower drift (the bay round the shaft) the mole
// wall-climbs a timber post, is handed onto the site's rope ladder as soon as the rope is beside it (W held),
// climbs to the rope's top end and hangs there (no bobbing off the end), and jumps east onto the upper heading.
// The mine is 72 m long and its mouths are at the far east end, so the scenario starts inside (the harness
// world is 128 m wide). Known layout blockers (sites.rs; see REFINE-movement.md): posts stand floor to roof
// every 4 m on both levels, so each bay is sealed and the mouths never reach the chest; the shaft's rope hangs
// 8 m from the upper floor and stops 4 m above the lower one, beside the west post.
map
